# === Copy this file to the repo root as ".gitignore" ===
# (The leading dot matters. Finder hides dotfiles by default:
#  toggle visibility with Cmd+Shift+.)

# --- Secrets / credentials (MOST IMPORTANT SECTION) ---
.Renviron
.Rprofile
*.env
.env
secrets.*
credentials.*
config_local.*
setConfigUser*.R          # files with personal paths and/or keys
!setConfigUser.example.R  # but keep the example template in the repo

# --- R session artifacts ---
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj.user
.quarto/

# --- macOS / editor clutter ---
.DS_Store
Icon?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Python / Jupyter ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Backup files ---
*.bak
*.R.bak
*~

# --- Large data & model outputs ---
# (GitHub hard-blocks files over 100 MB and warns above 50 MB.
#  Keeping total repo size under 1 GB is good practice.)
*.parquet
*.zip
*.bin
*.h5
*.pkl
*.sav

# --- Large rendered HTML output ---
# files like dashboard.html can be 5 MB+; publish those via GitHub Pages instead
*_cache/
*_files/
dashboard.html

# --- Exceptions: keep these in the repo ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!data/*_sample.csv
